<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n90490" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προτέμνω</span></b> , aor.
		<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προὔτᾰμον</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>cut off beforehand</i>, [
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὄψον] προταμών</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					9.489
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>cut off in front, cut short</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">κορμὸν ἐκ ῥίζης προταμών</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					23.196
				</span></i>
			; <i>prune</i> vines, <i><span class="en">
				<u>PLond.</u>
				1.131.375
			</span></i>, al. <span class="entity">(i A.D.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			
				Med.
			, <i>cut forward</i> or <i>in front</i> of one,
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εἰ ὦλκα διηνεκέα
			προταμοίμην</span> if in ploughing I <i>cut</i> an unbroken
			furrow <i>before me</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				18.375
			</span></i>; but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">προταμέσθαι ἀρούρας</span>
			<i>mow</i> them <i>before</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.R.
				3.1387
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
</div>